From 030139a4d5ac773420c1a55553874cc96762a53b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 23:37:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wire all 44 frontend API routes to real FastAPI backend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace every mock/stub Next.js API route with a real proxy to the
FastAPI backend. Previously, all frontend routes returned hardcoded
fake data — now they forward requests to the backend preserving
method, headers, query params, body, and auth tokens.

Changes:
- Add frontend/src/lib/backend-proxy.ts — shared proxy utility that
  forwards requests to BACKEND_URL (default http://localhost:8000)
- Replace all 44 route files under frontend/src/app/api/v1/ to use
  proxyToBackend() instead of returning mock data
- Chat route uses stream: true for SSE passthrough
- Dynamic routes ([id], [service]) pass context for param resolution
- File uploads (CSV import) forward raw body with content-type
- Add BACKEND_URL to .env.example documentation
- BACKEND_URL already configured in docker-compose.yml as http://backend:8000

The frontend is now a true client of the backend API, not a demo shell.

https://claude.ai/code/session_013VPx1ByRZU684nEDpz5cu6
